      "notes": "The published BindCraft image admits its AlphaFold2 mount only through artifact_gate.verify_manifest, which reads FS2_ARTIFACT_MANIFEST at /models/alphafold2/manifest.json and requires artifact_kind 'bindcraft-af2-params' and source_revision 7cd4ace1b7407adf66a50dfefa47de2270f5e4a9. Upstream ships no such document, so the sixteen-file upstream tree does not run that image as-is. This is a deliberately separate identity from alphafold2-params: same archive provenance, seventeen-entry tree, its own inventory digest, and a manifest bound by its own digest so a drifting generator fails closed. Proteina-Complexa must keep reading the sixteen-entry tree, because ColabDesign globs *.npz and an extra document there is not part of that contract. Materializing a second copy rather than overlaying the manifest onto the sixteen-entry tree costs one extra parameter set on disk, and buys a mount whose whole content is one verifiable identity."
    },
